# Reproducible cross-platform vendoring (spec 009).
#
# `@atlcli/pdf-compiler-browser` vendors the typst.ts wasm-bindgen glue AFTER
# Bun applies the CSP-hardening patch below. Bun's patch application copies the
# patch's added lines verbatim, so the patch file's own line endings end up in
# the vendored glue (`typst_ts_web_compiler.mjs`) whose sha256 is pinned in
# `TYPST_VENDOR_PINS`. If a contributor has `core.autocrlf=true` (the Windows
# default) git would check the patch out with CRLF, the patched glue bytes would
# differ from the LF-computed pin, and the `vendor:typst` postinstall would fail
# with a sha256 mismatch. Force LF on the patch (and on the vendored text glue,
# should it ever be committed) so the patched bytes are identical on
# macOS/Linux/Windows regardless of autocrlf.
patches/** text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.d.ts text eol=lf

# Binary assets must NEVER be line-ending normalized — normalization would
# corrupt them and the wasm/font sha pins depend on their exact bytes.
*.wasm binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
packages/**/fixtures/**/publication/assets/** binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.docx binary
*.dotx binary
*.xlsx binary
*.pptx binary
